{{!
    @template local_unifiedgrader/help_section_assign

    Help page partial: marking an assignment. The grader's help button links
    to #integration-assign, so that id must stay.

    Context variables:
    * img - object - Screenshot URLs keyed by file name in pix/help.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "img": {
            "blind_marking": "https://moodle.example.com/theme/image.php/boost/local_unifiedgrader/1/help/blind_marking",
            "feedback_comments_disabled": "https://moodle.example.com/theme/image.php/boost/local_unifiedgrader/1/help/feedback_comments_disabled",
            "file_and_online_text": "https://moodle.example.com/theme/image.php/boost/local_unifiedgrader/1/help/file_and_online_text",
            "stacked_dual_view": "https://moodle.example.com/theme/image.php/boost/local_unifiedgrader/1/help/stacked_dual_view",
            "word_conversion_failed": "https://moodle.example.com/theme/image.php/boost/local_unifiedgrader/1/help/word_conversion_failed",
            "word_converted": "https://moodle.example.com/theme/image.php/boost/local_unifiedgrader/1/help/word_converted"
        }
    }
}}
<section id="integration-assign" class="local-unifiedgrader-help-activity">
<h4 class="local-unifiedgrader-help-activity-title"><i class="fa fa-file-text-o" aria-hidden="true"></i> Assignments</h4>

<h5>What you see on the left</h5>
<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-table">
<table class="table-reboot">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">The student submitted</th><th scope="col">The preview shows</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">A PDF</th><td>The document with the full <a href="#feature-annotations">annotation toolbar</a>.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">A Word or other office file</th><td>A PDF copy made by a document converter enabled in Moodle, with the full toolbar.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">An image</th><td>The image, with the annotation tools.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Online text</th><td>With a converter and <em>Render online text as PDF</em> switched on: <em>Online text.pdf</em> with the full toolbar. Otherwise the text inline, with a reduced toolbar.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Audio or video</th><td>A player.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Several things</th><td>A pill for each above the marking panel: <strong>Submission</strong> for the online text, then one per file. Click a pill to switch. The download icon on a file pill saves the file.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
    <a href="{{img.file_and_online_text}}" data-action="help-zoom">
        <img src="{{img.file_and_online_text}}" width="1600" height="909" loading="lazy"
             alt="A submission with online text and a PDF file. Above the marking panel are three pills: Submission, Online text.pdf (selected) and sower-essay.pdf. Four layout buttons show in the header.">
    </a>
    <figcaption>A submission with online text and a file. The pills switch between them, and a
    fourth layout button, <strong>Dual file view</strong>, appears in the header.</figcaption>
</figure>

<p><strong>Dual file view</strong> stacks two sources one above the other, so you can read the
student's own text while you annotate the PDF. The lower pane is marked <em>Marking here</em>, and
you can drag the divider between them.</p>

<figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
    <a href="{{img.stacked_dual_view}}" data-action="help-zoom">
        <img src="{{img.stacked_dual_view}}" width="1600" height="909" loading="lazy"
             alt="Dual file view: the submission text in an upper pane and Online text.pdf in a lower pane labelled Marking here.">
    </a>
    <figcaption>Dual file view: two sources stacked, with the one you are marking below.</figcaption>
</figure>

<h5>When a file cannot be converted</h5>
<p>If the converter cannot be reached, the preview says <em>This file could not be converted to
PDF for preview.</em> with a <strong>Retry conversion</strong> button. Retry works as soon as the
converter is reachable again; you do not need to reload the page. If it keeps failing, tell your
administrator (see <a href="#troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</a>). You can still download the
file from its pill and grade as usual.</p>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shots">
    <figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
        <a href="{{img.word_conversion_failed}}" data-action="help-zoom">
            <img src="{{img.word_conversion_failed}}" width="1600" height="591" loading="lazy"
                 alt="An empty preview with the red message: This file could not be converted to PDF for preview, and a Retry conversion button.">
        </a>
        <figcaption>Conversion failed: the message and <strong>Retry conversion</strong>.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
        <a href="{{img.word_converted}}" data-action="help-zoom">
            <img src="{{img.word_converted}}" width="1600" height="727" loading="lazy"
                 alt="The same Word file, four-soils.docx, now shown as a PDF with the annotation toolbar above it.">
        </a>
        <figcaption>The same Word file after a successful retry, ready to annotate.</figcaption>
    </figure>
</div>

<h5>What you can do on the right</h5>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Grade</strong>: a number or a scale, or a <a href="#feature-rubrics">rubric or marking guide</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Overall Feedback</strong> in the editor, with images, audio and video
        (see <a href="#feature-grades">Grades and feedback</a>).</li>
    <li><strong>Feedback files</strong>: upload files for the student, when feedback files are enabled for the assignment.</li>
    <li><strong>Penalties</strong>, <strong>teacher notes</strong>, and the
        <a href="#feature-referral">academic integrity</a> button.</li>
    <li><strong>Attempts</strong>: when the student has more than one attempt, an attempt selector
        appears. Grades and feedback are saved against the attempt you are viewing.</li>
</ul>

<h5>Assignment settings the grader follows</h5>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Blind marking.</strong> Students appear as <em>Participant 1</em>,
        <em>Participant 2</em> and so on, in the header and in the student list.</li>
    <li><strong>Feedback comments switched off.</strong> The editor is replaced by the notice
        <em>Feedback comments are not enabled for this assessment</em>. You can still grade, annotate and attach files.</li>
    <li><strong>Group submissions.</strong> A team's work shows once, and the grade goes to every
        member, as in Moodle's own grading page.</li>
    <li><strong>Marking workflow.</strong> Posting a grade also releases it in the workflow.</li>
</ul>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shots">
    <figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
        <a href="{{img.blind_marking}}" data-action="help-zoom">
            <img src="{{img.blind_marking}}" width="1200" height="382" loading="lazy"
                 alt="The grader header on a blind-marked assignment. The student is shown as Participant 1.">
        </a>
        <figcaption>Blind marking: the student is <em>Participant 1</em>.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
        <a href="{{img.feedback_comments_disabled}}" data-action="help-zoom">
            <img src="{{img.feedback_comments_disabled}}" width="1200" height="750" loading="lazy"
                 alt="The marking panel with an amber notice under Overall Feedback: Feedback comments are not enabled for this assessment.">
        </a>
        <figcaption>Feedback comments switched off in the assignment settings.</figcaption>
    </figure>
</div>
</section>
